# Analects Book 19 (子張). Same format as the pilot (drafts/analects-01/units.py) and Book 18: one unit per stretch
# between Zhu Xi's commentary interruptions (33 units, 25 passages; the book has no running-head lemma). Drafted in
# two halves and reviewed as one book: UNITS_A = lemmata 0–19 (19.1–19.19), UNITS_B = lemmata 20–32 (19.20–19.25);
# UNITS = UNITS_A + UNITS_B, so UNITS[0] is lemma 0 and unit numbers below are UNITS indexes.
# Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (heading: 此篇皆記弟子之言而子夏為多子貢次之…凡二十五章; each ○ checked in
# the commentary file KR1h0015_009.txt): 19.1 = unit 0, 19.2 = 1, 19.3 = 2, 19.4 = 3, 19.5 = 4, 19.6 = 5, 19.7 = 6,
# 19.8 = 7, 19.9 = 8, 19.10 = 9, 19.11 = 10, 19.12 = 11–12 (Ziyou's charge, then Zixia's answer after Zhu Xi's
# comment), 19.13 = 13, 19.14 = 14, 19.15 = 15, 19.16 = 16, 19.17 = 17, 19.18 = 18, 19.19 = 19, 19.20 = 20,
# 19.21 = 21, 19.22 = 22–23, 19.23 = 24–27, 19.24 = 28, 19.25 = 29–32. (The ○ inside the comment after 仲尼焉學,
# 朝音潮焉於䖍反○公孫朝衞大夫, only parts Zhu Xi's sound marks from his gloss; it is not a chapter break.) Each
# stretch holds at most one chapter (no npas).
# Speakers: Zizhang 19.1–3, Zixia 19.3–13 (with Ziyou's charge in 19.12), Ziyou 19.14–15, Master Zeng 19.16–19,
# Zigong 19.20–25 — four sayings or answers of his own, two answers to men who set him above the Master (19.23,
# 19.25) and one to a man who ran the Master down (19.24).
# Line breaks: the lines of t (one more than the ^ breaks after the first token) equal the lines of l in
# every unit. Speech openers (子張曰：「, 子夏曰：「, 子貢曰：「 …) stand on a line of their own when the speech runs
# to more than one line (as Book 18). Quotation marks balance within every unit. Quote inside a quote: 『』 in w,
# ‘’ in l and i (unit 2, the disciples citing Zixia). 吾聞諸夫子 (units 17, 18) is followed by a colon, not an
# inner quote: there is no 曰, and the words are Master Zeng's report of the Master's sense. Where a speech runs on
# past one of Zhu Xi's comments the continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and English alike (as Books 17–18):
# 19.23 units 26–27 (Zigong, whose 子貢曰：「 opens in unit 25, closed at the end of that unit), 19.25 units 31–32
# (Zigong, opened and closed in unit 30). Each continuation note says whose words they are.
# 夫子, decided for the whole book: in a disciple's mouth it is the Master — l 'the Master' throughout; i 'the
#   Master' for Master Zeng (17, 18; as 4.15) and 'our Master' for Zigong (23, 26, 31, 32; as 1.10); in 27 it is
#   Shusun Wushu, 'that lord' (l; i 'his lordship'), as Jisun at 14.38.
# Cross-references cite the shipped passage numbers: 見危授命 (14.13) and 見得思義 (16.10) for 19.1; 子張 (2.18);
#   士 (4.9, 13.20); 𢎞 'broad' (8.7); 子夏 (1.7); 損友 (16.4); 異端 (2.16); 好學…也已 (1.14); 博學 (6.25, 12.15);
#   切切 (13.28); 在其中矣 (2.18, 15.31); 人之過也 (4.7); 溫而厲 (7.37); 即 (13.29); 不踰矩 (2.4); 子游 (2.7);
#   抑 (14.33); 誨人不倦 (7.2); 一以貫之 (4.15); 噫 'hm!', 心不平聲 (13.20); 行有餘力則以學文 (1.6); 優 (14.12);
#   喪與其易也寧戚 (3.4); 師也過 (11.15); 曾子 (1.4, 14.28); 剛毅木訥近仁 (13.27); 為仁 (1.2); 必也…乎 (3.7,
#   12.13, 13.3); 三年無改於父之道 (1.11, 4.20); 諒隂 (14.43); 孟孫 (2.5); 季孟 (18.3); 士師 (18.2); 紂 Zhou,
